From 02a14193d7c3d3d5713b6d67ed81dcdcda04c9e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:02:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - drop the four-byte scatterlist offset check

Do not bounce a read-only source solely because its offset is not a
multiple of four. The packet-engine manual's four-byte ESP padding
minimum describes packet length and does not establish a DMA buffer
address requirement for the basic operations used by this driver.

Remove the explicit offset check. Keep the cipher-block length checks
and cache-line isolation for DMA-written and in-place buffers. Update
the comment to describe the remaining source checks accurately.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 eip93-common.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eip93-common.c b/eip93-common.c
index 07c490d..5826ec3 100644
--- a/eip93-common.c
+++ b/eip93-common.c
@@ -213,12 +213,9 @@ static bool eip93_is_sg_aligned(struct scatterlist *sg, u32 len,
 	int nents;
 
 	for (nents = 0; sg; sg = sg_next(sg), ++nents) {
-		if (!IS_ALIGNED(sg->offset, 4))
-			return false;
-
 		/*
 		 * DMA-written buffers must not share cache lines with CPU writes.
-		 * Read-only sources only need the hardware alignment checks.
+		 * Read-only sources do not need cache-line isolation.
 		 * dma_map_sg() maps the entire entry, including any bytes beyond
 		 * the requested crypt length in the last entry.
 		 */
